Description: Let an external client draw the window switcher session
 labwc keeps the window switcher session (chord, order, selection, commit on
 modifier release). This adds zlabwc_window_switcher_renderer_v1, a private
 protocol offered only to the one client labwc launches itself on a
 pre-connected socket (<windowSwitcher renderer="command">), and again as soon as
 it exits (at most every 5 s). The renderer is told
 the session and may only ask to move the selection. If it has not acknowledged
 a session within 300 ms, or is gone, labwc draws its own OSD as before.
 Text keys labwc does not use during a session are handed to the renderer.
 Version 2 adds pictures: the renderer may ask for a listed window, which labwc
 renders offscreen from the window's own scene subtree (as upstream labwc's
 thumbnail switcher, src/cycle/osd-thumbnail.c, does; at twice the size and
 averaged down 2x2 when it shrinks by 2 or more) and hands over in a sealed
 memory file, at most 15 a second. A screen lock ends the session, and no
 window is captured or selected behind one. While the renderer draws the session, a
 held Tab steps every 0.7 s (each window stays in front that long)
 instead of at the keyboard's repeat rate.
 Built for Yantrik OS's Alt+Tab (yantrikos/yantrik-os#867, #849).
Author: Yantrik OS <dev@yantrikos.com>
Forwarded: not-yet
Last-Update: 2026-10-20
Reviewed-by: security reviews of yantrikos/yantrik-os#872 (findings 1-5 addressed) and #876 (lock finding fixed)
